Day 008 - Classes and Objects

Class : A class is a blueprint that defines fields (data) and methods (behavior).

Object : An object is an instance of a class created with new.

java
class Student {
    int id;
    String name;

    void display() {
        System.out.println(id + " " + name);
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Student s1 = new Student();
        s1.id = 1;
        s1.name = "Ravi";
        s1.display();
    }
}

Memory
Area	    Stores
Stack	    Local variables, references
Heap	    Objects

Student s1 = new Student(); → s1 (reference) lives on the stack, the object on the heap.

